With DLSS Performance or Ultra Performance, the pre-scene targets of 0162 that the scene's own draws sample (a texture
resolved from them bound by scene draws in three frames) are drawn at the game's own scale, 1x, instead of the scene's:
the smallest they can be without going below the original. The others stay at the scene's scale, and one drawn into
or sampled after the scene stays at the full one for the session, as before. Their resolves stretch them back to the
full size the same way, and their depth bias keeps the game's own slope scale (the command processor takes it from
the draw's adjustment). d3d12_dlss_pre_scene_native (on) turns it off. Builds on 0163.

